rounds.answer1:
Identity verification systems integrate cryptographically-signed temporal constraints by:  
- Generating a **time-bound, one-time token** (e.g., TOTP or signed JWT) upon user request;  
- Embedding a **timestamp and expiration window** (e.g., 5 minutes) in the token;  
- Signing the token with a **server-side key** to ensure integrity and authenticity;  
- Transmitting it via **secure, out-of-band channels** (e.g., email, SMS, authenticator app);  
- Validating the token **server-side** with strict time checks and one-time use enforcement.  

This ensures only the legitimate user—having access to the verified channel and acting within the time window—can reset credentials, preventing replay and impersonation.

