Residual smartphone data retains physical recoverability after logical deletion when:  
- **TRIM commands are disabled or not executed** (common in older Android/iOS versions);  
- **Data has not been overwritten** by new writes or garbage collection;  
- **Wear-leveling algorithms have not migrated or erased the blocks**;  
- **Storage is not encrypted at the hardware level** (or encryption key is accessible);  
- **The device is powered off or disconnected**, preventing automatic data scrubbing.  

Recovery is most likely within days to weeks post-deletion, before system activity overwrites the blocks. Forensic tools can extract data from unallocated or slack space if these conditions hold.

