- Spoofed sender addresses;  
- Urgent or deceptive subject lines;  
- Malicious links or attachments;  
- Impersonation of trusted entities (e.g., banks, IT support, colleagues).  

Other vectors include SMS (smishing), voice calls (vishing), and fake login pages. Email remains dominant due to widespread use, low cost, and high success rate in tricking users into revealing credentials or downloading malware.

